5,Gyalsumdo Language (GYO) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/gyo/,"Gyalsumdo is an endangered indigenous language of Nepal. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by adults only.",Gyalsumdo,Sino-Tibetan
6,"(PDF) Preliminary Notes on Gyalsumdo, an Undocumented Tibetan...",https://www.academia.edu/773414/Preliminary_Notes_on_Gyalsumdo_an_Undocumented_Tibetan_Variety_in_Manang_District_Nepal,Gyalsumdo is hypothesized to belong to the Central Tibetan branch of the Tibeto-Burman family. Approximately 164 lexical items were recorded to analyze Gyalsumdo's linguistic features.,Gyalsumdo,Sino-Tibetan
7,Gyalsumdo Project | Mandala Collections - Audio-Video,https://av.mandala.library.virginia.edu/collection/gyalsumdo-project,"Gyalsumdo is a variety of Tibetan that is spoken in a cluster of villages in the lower Manang District of Nepal (Gandaki Zone, 22° 59’ N; 84° 22’ E). There is currently no ISO 639 code assigned to Gyalsumdo.",Gyalsumdo,Sino-Tibetan
